\( \begin{array}{l}a\rightarrow\times 3\rightarrow+4\rightarrow4+3 a \\ a\rightarrow+4\rightarrow\times 3\rightarrow3(4+a)\end{array} \)

generated reasoning trace:
A function machine applies the operations in order from left to right.

- First pair: start with \(a\), then multiply by \(3\), giving \(3a\). Then add \(4\), giving \(3a+4\), which is the same as \(4+3a\). So this machine is correct:
\[
a\rightarrow\times 3\rightarrow+4\rightarrow4+3 a
\]

- Second pair: start with \(a\), then add \(4\), giving \(a+4\). Then multiply by \(3\), giving \(3(a+4)\), which is the same as \(3(4+a)\). So this machine is also correct:
\[
a\rightarrow+4\rightarrow\times 3\rightarrow3(4+a)
\]

Therefore, the correct pairs of function machines are
\[
\begin{array}{l}
a\rightarrow\times 3\rightarrow+4\rightarrow4+3 a \\
a\rightarrow+4\rightarrow\times 3\rightarrow3(4+a)
\end{array}
\]

