question:
The median of these four numbers is \( 5 \).
\(
\begin{array}{cccc}
3&12&1&?
\end{array}
\)
Find the value of the missing number.

correct answer:
\( 7 \)

generated reasoning trace:
For four numbers, the median is the average of the two middle numbers after ordering them from least to greatest.

The known numbers are \(1, 3, 12,\) and \(?\). To make the median \(5\), the missing number must fit between \(3\) and \(12\), so the middle two numbers will be \(3\) and \(?\).

Then:
\[
\frac{3+?}{2}=5
\]

Multiply by \(2\):
\[
3+?=10
\]

Subtract \(3\):
\[
?=7
\]

The value of the missing number is \( 7 \).

