\[
h(j+2)=15\cdot 5=75
\]

Also,
\[
2+j=2+3=5
\]
So
\[
h(2+j)=15\cdot 5=75
\]

Since addition is commutative, \(j+2\) and \(2+j\) are equal, so both statements are true.

The correct answer is \( \begin{array}{l}h(j+2)=75 \\ h(2+j)=75\end{array} \).

