Inequality \( 1 \) & Inequality 2 \\
\( 2 d>11 \) & \( 11>d+2 \)
\end{tabular}

correct answer:
Only Inequality \( 2 \)

generated reasoning trace:
Substitute \( d=5 \) into each inequality.

For Inequality 1:
\[
2d>11 \Rightarrow 2(5)>11 \Rightarrow 10>11
\]
This is false.

For Inequality 2:
\[
11>d+2 \Rightarrow 11>5+2 \Rightarrow 11>7
\]
This is true.

So \( d=5 \) could satisfy only the second inequality. The correct answer is: Only Inequality \( 2 \).

