But being a multiple of \(10\) does not mean it is a multiple of \(25\). For example, \(10\) is a common multiple of \(2\) and \(5\), and \(10\) is not a multiple of \(25\).

So common multiples of \(2\) and \(5\) are not multiples of \(25\), which means the statement is never true.

