\(10\% \times 150 = 15\).

Add that on:
\(240 + 15 = 255\).

Now compare £255 to the original £150:
\(\frac{255}{150} = 1.7\).

So the amount is \(170\%\) of the original, and adding the percentage increases \(60\% + 10\% = 70\%\), but since the second increase is only based on the original amount, this gives \(166\%\) of the original.

