Then \(490 - 49 = 441\).

Katie’s method starts with \(50 \times 9\), but changing \(49\) to \(50\) changes the calculation, so that compensation doesn’t work this way.  
\(50 \times 9 = 450\), and subtracting \(9\) is not a valid way to get back to \(49 \times 9\).

So only Tom would get the correct answer.

