misconception:
Believes a direct proportion graph does not have to start at the origin

generated reasoning trace:
Since £1 = 1.5 US dollars, I need a graph that goes up in a straight line by 1.5 dollars for every 1 pound.

At £10, the value would be 10 × 1.5 = 15 dollars, so the line should reach about (10, 15).

Because it is a constant rate, I look for a straight line. I don’t think it has to start at 0, so a straight line that goes through the point near (10, 15) is fine.

So I choose the graph with a straight line starting around 5 on the y-axis and rising to 15.

